1.  the coupling and response of the channel, symbolically
====================================================================================================================
  F(y)   = 2*(y + 1)*exp(-y) - 2
  F'(y)  = -2*y*exp(-y)
  F''(y) = 2*(y - 1)*exp(-y)
  [PASS] T1 the MOND channel's coupling F'(y) and linear response F''(y) both carry an explicit factor e^{-y}: they are not power-suppressed at high acceleration, they are exponentially suppressed   (F'/e^-y = -2*y, F''/e^-y = 2*y - 2)
  [PASS] T2 the small-y limit is MOND (F'' -> -2, the deep-MOND cubic sits at cubic order) and the large-y limit is exactly GR (F' -> 0, F'' -> 0, F -> -2 a constant absorbed into Lambda): the same function does both   (F''(0) = -2; F'(inf) = 0; F(inf) = -2)

