====================================================================================================================
  fractional anomaly at Saturn: simple mu -> 1.436e-06 (a power-law 1/y tail);  exponential mu -> 0e+00
  Cassini bound on an anomalous fractional acceleration at Saturn is of order 1e-9 to 1e-8 (ephemeris/ranging)
  [PASS] M1 mutation: replacing the exponential with the simple 1/(1+x) kernel gives a POWER-LAW tail 1/y, a fractional anomaly of 1e-6 at Saturn -- two to three orders above the ranging bound -- reproducing the known Cassini kill of the simple function.  The invisibility is a property of the exponential tail specifically, not of MOND kernels in general   (simple: 1.44e-06 (killed); exponential: 0e+00 (invisible))
  [PASS] M2 mutation: the theorem is footing-independent because y at every site exceeds 1e5 on both footings, and e^{-1e5} is zero for any purpose   (y(Saturn) = 6.96e+05 canonical, 5.77e+05 alt)

====================================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  The pincer's last link is gone: alpha_3 = O(1) for the constraint branch was never derived and is withdrawn.
  This file shows it could not have been derived as a kill, for this kernel: the MOND channel couples through
  F_exp(y), whose coupling and response are suppressed by e^{-y}, and y exceeds 7e5 at Saturn and 1e12 at a binary
  pulsar.  Every PPN parameter the channel could contribute to is suppressed below 1e-300000 at every test site.
  The constraint branch -- CDE-L4C, HPI-Delta, the smoothly-vanishing spatial projector -- has GR's PPN status and
  no solar-system or pulsar measurement can ever change that.  The same tail that saves the kernel at Cassini
  saves the constraint channel everywhere it is tested.
  What closes the branch is therefore ONE gate: no instantaneous physical channel, a causality principle resting
  on the York/CMC external-field argument at medium confidence.  The no-go for two-degree-of-freedom MOND is a
  causality theorem, not a data exclusion, and the paper's section 3.1 and the projector verdict are corrected to
  say so.  The aether kill is untouched: its alpha_1 lives in an F-independent kinetic sector.

